    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete and minimal.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked to derive an owner's `locality` from its city (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD; `UNKNOWN` otherwise) and expose it on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nI followed the codebase's established pattern for derived owner fields (`householdId`, `customerCode`, etc.), which keeps structural impact low:\n\n1. **New file `LocalityResolver.java`** \u2014 a small, self-contained helper (like `HouseholdMatcher`/`NamesakeCounter`) with a single `locality(city)` method backed by a fixed map. Zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0), CC = 1.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` read-only property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` annotation line on `toOwnerDto`, delegating to the new helper. The method body isn't touched and the mapping logic lives entirely in the tiny cohesive class.\n\nNo existing method grew in complexity; the behavior is added as an isolated unit. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `AcceptanceTest` including both `coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`).",
